WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.218
- [Narrator] Once you find
out what it is that moves

00:00:03.218 --> 00:00:07.385
and shakes you don't want
to do or be anything else.

00:00:08.344 --> 00:00:10.609
And though I lost my ability to speak,

00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:12.442
I never lost my voice.

00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:15.940
So I'm a filmmaker with
motor neuron disease.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.129
- [Woman] How long have
have I been asleep?

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:18.629
Where have I been?

00:00:20.296 --> 00:00:22.811
And nothing is recognizable.

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:24.881
- [Narrator] Eight years
ago, Simon Fitzmaurice

00:00:24.881 --> 00:00:25.919
was an up-and-coming film director.

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:26.752
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:27.954
But just as his career was taking off,

00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:32.077
he was diagnosed with motor
neuron disease, or MND,

00:00:32.077 --> 00:00:35.001
a degenerative condition
also known as ALS.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.881
Doctors told him he had
only four years to live.

00:00:37.881 --> 00:00:40.261
- [Simon] Every profession is inconvenient

00:00:40.261 --> 00:00:42.159
to motor neuron disease.

00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:45.190
But we don't choose what
moves us, what drives us,

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.170
it chooses us.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.779
It's up to you what you
choose to do about it.

00:00:49.779 --> 00:00:52.658
- [Narrator] He chose
to fight his diagnosis.

00:00:52.658 --> 00:00:55.039
He learned to speak through a
computer and went on to write

00:00:55.039 --> 00:00:57.166
and direct his first feature film.

00:00:57.166 --> 00:00:59.186
- [Simon] When all this
happened, it was my writing

00:00:59.186 --> 00:01:00.661
that saved me.

00:01:00.661 --> 00:01:04.255
Like writing, the passion
of film has never left me.

00:01:04.255 --> 00:01:08.142
‘My Name is Emily’ is both
of my passions combined.

00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:11.540
So MND made me even more
determined to direct this film.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:15.639
MND is defined by loss,
by what it takes away.

00:01:15.639 --> 00:01:18.389
But this was me taking something back.

00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:21.149
I can write the
script, I can storyboard,

00:01:21.149 --> 00:01:23.649
choose frames with my DP.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.531
I can make all the hundreds of decisions

00:01:25.531 --> 00:01:27.297
that comprise this job.

00:01:27.297 --> 00:01:29.846
The biggest challenge
in filmmaking that comes

00:01:29.846 --> 00:01:31.263
with MND is time.

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:34.211
When I'm on set, there's
a short delay while I type

00:01:34.211 --> 00:01:35.461
up my thoughts.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.085
I overcome this by preparing
as much as possible

00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:42.085
in advance of the shoot.

00:01:42.965 --> 00:01:43.798
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:01:43.798 --> 00:01:45.557
- [Narrator] Simon and his
wife have had three children

00:01:45.557 --> 00:01:47.857
since his diagnosis.

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:50.311
He says he wants to keep
creating to show his children

00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:52.921
the importance of never giving up.

00:01:52.921 --> 00:01:54.980
- [Simon] When you love films as I do,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.849
you simply want to
contribute, to add my voice

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.766
to the art form I love.

00:01:59.937 --> 00:02:02.454
I once thought of MND as
a prison camp to which

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:05.371
no liberating army would ever come.

00:02:06.311 --> 00:02:08.081
But I outgrew the prison.

00:02:08.081 --> 00:02:08.998
I am free.

